\":\"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/7660a6dae5a26ff506f0be04c3c35807480f565ca201c63311fd4bfa47ff02a0?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"caption\":\"Ashima Jain\"},\"description\":\"Ashima Jain is a Content Editor and Strategist with 6 years of experience in content marketing. She specializes in content planning, editing, and optimization, ensuring every piece is accurate, well-structured, and aligned with user search intent. Her work is guided by in-depth research, editorial best practices, and SEO principles to create high-quality, reader-focused resources that deliver value.\",\"sameAs\":[\"https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/in\/ashimajain90\/\"],\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/author\/ashima\/\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710772495099\",\"position\":1,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710772495099\",\"name\":\"1. How does PPC work?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Advertisers bid on keywords relevant to their target market. When a user searches for that keyword, the search engine or platform displays ads based on who has bid the most and whose ad is most relevant to the search query. You pay the bid amount only when someone clicks on your ad.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786356024\",\"position\":2,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786356024\",\"name\":\"2. Where do PPC ads appear?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"PPC ads can appear on search engines like Google or Bing, social media platforms like Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn, and other websites participating in advertising networks.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786374340\",\"position\":3,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786374340\",\"name\":\"3. How much does PPC advertising cost?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The cost of PPC advertising varies widely based on factors like the competitiveness of the keywords you're bidding on, the quality of your ads, and your target audience. You set your budget, so costs can range from a few dollars a day to thousands per month.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786391092\",\"position\":4,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786391092\",\"name\":\"4. What is a Quality Score in PPC?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Quality Score is a metric used by Google Ads to assess the relevance and quality of your PPC ads and keywords. It affects your ad placement and the cost per click (CPC). A higher Quality Score means lower costs and better ad positions.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786415059\",\"position\":5,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786415059\",\"name\":\"5. Can I do PPC advertising on a small budget?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, PPC advertising can be effective even on a small budget. It's important to focus on highly targeted keywords, monitor your campaigns closely, and optimize based on performance to get the most out of your investment.<br\/>\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786448405\",\"position\":6,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786448405\",\"name\":\"6. How do I choose the right keywords for my PPC campaigns?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Keyword research involves understanding your target audience, using keyword research tools (like Google Keyword Planner), analyzing competitors, and selecting keywords that are relevant to your products or services and have a good balance of search volume and competition.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786466735\",\"position\":7,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786466735\",\"name\":\"7. What is the difference between PPC and SEO?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"PPC is a paid strategy where you pay for each click on your ad, while SEO (Search Engine Optimization) focuses on improving your website and content to rank higher in organic search results. Both strategies aim to increase visibility and traffic but through different methods.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786484195\",\"position\":8,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/#faq-question-1710786484195\",\"name\":\"8. How can I measure the success of my PPC campaigns?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Success can be measured using metrics such as Click-Through Rate (CTR), Cost Per Click (CPC), Conversion Rate, and Return on Ad Spend (ROAS). These metrics help you understand how effectively your ads are reaching your audience and converting clicks into desired actions.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"}]}<\/script>\n<!-- \/ Yoast SEO plugin. -->","yoast_head_json":{"title":"What is PPC in Digital Marketing? A Beginner's Gui